    "narrative": "Our strongest play today is clearly **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who leads the Austin Waves with an elite 74.56 efficiency score. Batting second against Holmes, he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against a pitcher with a 4.71 xERA, combined with a significant platoon advantage that boosts his output projection by 14%. Similarly, **Jacob Wilson** (60.30) and **Heliot Ramos** (59.90) are high-value starts today; **Jacob Wilson** leverages a 10% park factor adjustment and a prime spot in the #2 hole, while **Heliot Ramos** capitalizes on the favorable 4.36 xERA of Sears and a strong batting order placement. While **Kyle Tucker** (58.62) falls just shy of the 60+ threshold, his elite base projection remains a cornerstone of our lineup, anchoring the lower middle-order.\n\nThe primary bench dilemma centered on the utility slot, as **Nasim Nunez** (56.82) provided a compelling case for inclusion based on his efficiency against Holmes and his aggressive base-running profile. Given that stolen bases are our highest priority, **Nasim Nunez** was nearly elevated, but he was edged out by the superior power-hitting metrics of our starting outfielders. Meanwhile, we continue to manage the absence of key contributors like **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Cole Carrigg**, who are all unavailable due to scheduled off-days, and **Jordan Westburg**, who remains sidelined on the IL. We are closely monitoring **Luis Robert Jr.** (47.30); while his score is bolstered by his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries\u2014a major asset for our SB-heavy strategy\u2014his platoon disadvantage against P\u00e9rez suggests a potential volatility risk. We have no active weather concerns, but owners should watch for any late lineup shifts affecting **Drake Baldwin**, whose #1 spot and strong xwOBA make him a vital component of today's scoring floor.",
